Disagreements with the reviewers (not applied):
 · a#2's ACCEPTED phrasing "Vi svarer for at kunne prøve…" keeps the German "svare for" (= vouch for/be liable),
   which is the very defect the row reports; the reviewer's own suggestion ("Vi vender tilbage for at undersøge…")
   is the correct Danish and is what was written.
 · a#46 proposed adding a [Kontakt](/da/contact) link inside a body paragraph of 003. Not applied: link count and
   hrefs must stay identical to the source. The CTA was rewritten in prose instead.
 · b#9's ACCEPTED value "ansættelsesbonus/underskriftsbonus" — used "underskriftsbonus (簽約金)" per ACCEPTED;
   the reviewer's "ansættelsesbonus" is vaguer and was not used.
 · b#10's "underafdelinger" reads like an internal org unit; "andre forretningsenheder (分支機構)" was used, which
   matches R8 ("branch establishment, generic").
 · b#48's "trusteeen (受託人)" is not Danish; "forvalteren (受託人)" (the reviewer's own alternative) was used.
 · b#16: the reviewer's "tilsynsførende" was applied, but the second sentence he calls a repeat ("uden revisor")
   is about a different body and was rewritten rather than deleted.
 · 016 "Nej."-openings: the reviewer proposed deleting the word only; the headings were left untouched (heading
   count is gated) and the first sentence made self-standing, which R7b allows.

A checker artefact worth recording for the next lane: findEnglishSentences() flags any ≥12-word sentence whose
Latin-only text contains ≥3 of {at, for, by, have}. Danish "at"/"for" trip it easily, and "5. juni" additionally
splits a sentence for that counter. Three rewrites (003, 004, 007) and one in 014 were re-phrased for this reason
only — meaning unchanged.

